{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1503, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given an integer array nums and a positive integer k. Return the sum of the maximum and minimum elements of all subsequences of nums with at most k elements.\nSince the answer may be very large, return it modulo 10^9 + 7.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: nums = [1,2,3], k = 2\nOutput: 24\nExplanation:\nThe subsequences of nums with at most 2 elements are:\n\n\n\nSubsequence \nMinimum\nMaximum\nSum\n\n\n[1]\n1\n1\n2\n\n\n[2]\n2\n2\n4\n\n\n[3]\n3\n3\n6\n\n\n[1, 2]\n1\n2\n3\n\n\n[1, 3]\n1\n3\n4\n\n\n[2, 3]\n2\n3\n5\n\n\nFinal Total\n \n \n24\n\n\n\nThe output would be 24.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: nums = [5,0,6], k = 1\nOutput: 22\nExplanation: \nFor subsequences with exactly 1 element, the minimum and maximum values are the element itself. Therefore, the total is 5 + 5 + 0 + 0 + 6 + 6 = 22.\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput: nums = [1,1,1], k = 2\nOutput: 12\nExplanation:\nThe subsequences [1, 1] and [1] each appear 3 times. For all of them, the minimum and maximum are both 1. Thus, the total is 12.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= nums.length <= 10^5\n0 <= nums[i] <= 10^9\n1 <= k <= min(70, nums.length)\n\n### Format: You will use the following starter code to write the solution to the problem and enclose your code within delimiters.\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def minMaxSums(self, nums: List[int], k: int) -> int:\n        \n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1544, "char_start": 1515, "quote": "Input:\n[1, 2, 3]\n2\nOutput:\n24", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1585, "char_start": 1556, "quote": "Input:\n[5, 0, 6]\n1\nOutput:\n22", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1626, "char_start": 1597, "quote": "Input:\n[1, 1, 1]\n2\nOutput:\n12", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "e5bc6418cdbd5afcea4b49a24bf6bf67e3e6bb959d3d0714763b443041a9284b", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "bae70e637080443b28f0c5d06cf38f6ad27db43486f603e8667dd11c80b49e6b", "seq": 2}
